# 11 - Generics and Type Constraints

## What is it?
Introduced in Go 1.18, Generics enable writing functions and data structures with type parameters.
- Type parameters are declared in square brackets: `func Map[T, U any](s []T, f func(T) U) []U`
- Constraints restrict the allowable types:
  - `any`: Alias for `interface{}` (all types allowed).
  - `comparable`: Any type supporting `==` and `!=` (usable as map keys).
  - Union constraints: `~int | ~int64 | ~float64` (the `~` matches underlying types).

---

